2026-09-27T12:05:51.7412272Z Update Note
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7412544Z ===========
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7412927Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7413307Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7413437Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7413720Z ================
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7413887Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7414089Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7414589Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7414888Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7415037Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7415416Z ====================================
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7415653Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7415799Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7416231Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7416628Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7417360Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7418201Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7418318Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7418812Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7419400Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7419713Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7420044Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7420492Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7420588Z Packages
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7420791Z ========
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7420909Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7422338Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7423863Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7424084Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7424601Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7425468Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7426111Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7491918Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7492874Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7493967Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7494137Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7494524Z ==========================
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7494804Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7496578Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7498775Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7499885Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7501463Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T12:05:51.7501834Z 
